  "result": "The settings page (`src/app/(dashboard)/[orgSlug]/settings/webhooks/page.tsx`) sends the new endpoint to `createWebhookAction`.\n\n- **Where the decision is made:** `src/actions/webhooks/create-webhook.ts`. It reads the plan's limits with `getPlanLimits(organization.plan)`, lists the endpoints the org already has, and throws `PlanLimitError(\"webhooks\", ...)` if `existing.length >= limits.webhooks`. This runs before the endpoint is created, so it is the check that refuses the customer.\n- **Where the number is declared:** `src/config/plan-limits.ts`. It sets the `webhooks` limit for each plan (for example `0` on free, `UNLIMITED` on the top tier).\n\nThere is a second, overlapping check: `createWebhook` in `src/server/services/webhook-service.ts` (line 62) calls `wouldExceedLimit(org.plan, \"webhooks\", used)`. When the request comes from this UI, the action's check refuses first, so I left the service file out of the answer.\n\nANSWER: src/actions/webhooks/create-webhook.ts, src/config/plan-limits.ts",
